; The CLI's own half of the executable (F3.2): every part of [bin/main.ml] that
; was a decision rather than an effect, in one library the suites can drive.
;
; [bin/main.ml] keeps three things only — which verb or flag set this invocation
; is, the [Eio_main] loop and [Eio.Stdenv.t] the grants are opened on, and the
; process's exit status. Everything the old 1000-line file also did (the server
; flag scanner, the client's argument scan and request bodies, the human
; rendering, the [--check] and [--metrics] reports, the startup validation) is
; here, takes its input and its network as arguments, and hands a value back
; instead of calling [exit]. That is what makes each of them testable, and it is
; why no module in this directory names a stream at all: [test/log_guard] keeps
; stderr behind [lib/log.ml] and [bin/main.ml].
;
; The direction is the one [lib/dune] states: this library links [seekwright] and
; [seekwright.factory] (the diagnosis builds providers and probes them), and
; nothing links it except [bin/] and the suites.
(library
 (name seekwright_cli)
 (public_name seekwright.cli)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries
  seekwright
  seekwright.factory
  mcp-caps
  eio
  ; [Cli_serve] waits on a self-pipe fd, so it names the unix sublibrary and
  ; stdlib Unix rather than relying on what [eio_main] happens to pull in.
  eio.unix
  unix
  eio_main
  uri
  yojson
  cohttp-eio
  http
  tls
  tls-eio
  ca-certs
  domain-name))
